{"step_index":369,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-26T07:33:47Z","content":"I have updated [`vercel.json`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/vercel.json) to restore Vercel's zero-config CDN static page serving.\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 Explanation\nWhen the `\"builds\"` section was included, Vercel disabled its default static file scanner, causing `/` to return a 404. Removing `\"builds\"` allows Vercel's Edge CDN to immediately serve all static frontend pages (`/`, `/checkout`, `/library`, CSS, JS, images, media) while routing `/api/*` to Python (`api/index.py`).\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Push the Fix to GitHub & Vercel\n\nRun these commands in Command Prompt:\n\n```cmd\ngit add .\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit commit -m \"fix: Restore Vercel zero-config CDN static route serving\"\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit push origin main\n```\n\nYour live site (`https://streamwave-gamma.vercel.app`) will re-deploy and load your landing page, checkout, and member library!"}
